# `make env` from the repo root turns this into a .env. Compose reads that .env
# from the project directory on its own, so
# nothing has to be exported in the shell or forwarded through the Makefile.
#
# .env is gitignored by bare name at any depth. This is a public repository:
# verify with `git check-ignore -v sites/logging.bythewood.me/.env`.

# There is no password here any more. Signing in happens on auth.bythewood.me,
# which pushes a code to a phone, and this site asks that one whether the cookie
# in a request is a live session.

# Write-only ntfy token for publishing silence and restart alerts, minted by
# `make ntfy-token`. It can publish to the alert topics and can read
# nothing, so this is the least useful secret here to steal. Unset means alerts
# are logged and never delivered; the site still starts, because an alerter that
# cannot deliver must never stop the checks that noticed the outage.
NTFY_TOKEN=
